    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the undisputed centerpiece of our lineup. Sporting an elite efficiency score of 81.87, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive confluence of variables: a favorable matchup against Littell, a strong ballpark, and a significant 3% boost from his extensive historical BvP success. While **Josh Lowe** sits lower in the batting order, his 71.68 score remains a priority start due to the high-upside combination of a weak opposing xERA and favorable wind conditions, which we are heavily leveraging to offset the inherent volatility of an 8-hole assignment. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** remains a high-floor play at 69.73; his plate discipline against Bradish and a 14% dynamic platoon advantage make him a foundational piece for maintaining our batting average categories.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Coby Mayo**, who finished with a competitive score of 60.58. Despite benefiting from the same positive park factors as other starters, **Coby Mayo** ultimately fell behind the rest of the infield corps due to a negative platoon split and a lower projected lineup slot, which cap his ceiling compared to the primary options like **Nolan Schanuel** or **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** We also considered **Wade Meckler** and **Curtis Mead**, but their projections lacked the necessary efficiency to displace the current outfield configuration. We are monitoring **Jackson Merrill** closely; despite his 58.90 score\u2014the lowest among our starters\u2014the risk of his sub-par platoon split against Sheehan is mitigated by the wind, keeping him in the mix as we chase volume in a high-scoring environment.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus given that some lineups are still pending, though we have factored in historical trends to project our order. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Jackson Merrill**, whose 14% negative SP skill adjustment is the most concerning variable on the board. Conversely, the aggressive baserunning potential provided by **Sam Antonacci** and **Kyle Tucker**\u2014both of whom are slotted into critical roles today\u2014remains our hedge against the scarcity of the SB category. As always, these starters represent our best path toward maximizing the 5x5 categories while remaining mindful of our game cap constraints.",
